  "paper": {
    "paper_id": "2212.02387",
    "title": "An Efficient Stochastic Algorithm for Decentralized Nonconvex-Strongly-Concave Minimax Optimization",
    "sha256": "a439c27a31fbadb3eec10c869bfdf653b88c4b01bf0b15cab6595c835b7b841a"
  },
  "algorithm": {
    "name": "DREAM (Decentralized Recursive-gradient dEscent Ascent Method)",
    "citations": [
      "PDF p.3, Algorithm 1: accelerated FastMix recurrence and output a^(K).",
      "PDF pp.3-4, Assumptions 2.1-2.5: lower bounded primal, average smoothness, local strong concavity, oracle conditions, symmetric PSD doubly stochastic W.",
      "PDF p.5, Definitions 2.4-2.5: rowwise projection onto the closed convex Y.",
      "PDF p.6, Algorithm 2 lines 3-8: consensus initialization and mixed initial full-gradient tracker.",
      "PDF p.6, Algorithm 2 lines 10-23: state update, Bernoulli refresh, omega/(bq) paired stochastic gradient differences and branch-specific tracker FastMix.",
      "PDF p.6, Algorithm 2 line 25: uniform output over all local x at times 0 through T-1.",
      "PDF p.7, Equations (5), (7), (8): sufficient theorem parameters, distinguished here from freely supplied Algorithm 2 inputs.",
      "PDF p.13, Lemma A.4: mean(s_t)=mean(g_t)."
    ],
    "core_mechanisms": [
      "two_timescale_gda",
      "projection_before_consensus",
      "fastmix_acceleration",
      "recursive_sample_difference",
      "bernoulli_agent_gating",
      "full_gradient_refresh",
      "recursive_gradient_tracking",
      "branch_specific_tracker_mixing",
      "uniform_historical_output"
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      "All tests are offline finite-sum problems; b_prime=n, uniform components. All local mean objectives are smooth and strongly concave in y; primal is lower bounded.",
      "Two agents, one x coordinate and one y coordinate, row-major state [x,y]. W has eigenvalues 1 and 0.8 and meets symmetry, irreducibility, double stochasticity and PSD assumptions.",
      "Randomness is conditioned on explicitly supplied realizations; output_draw_index is an explicit uniform-index realization, not an assertion about a particular RNG seed.",
      "FastMix indexing ambiguity: PDF Algorithm 1 loops k=0,...,K but explicitly returns a^(K). Contract follows the returned-state expression, hence K effective recurrences; any discarded extra a^(K+1) does not affect output. A differing loop-count convention should be reported as ambiguous rather than silently counted as a mathematical failure.",
      "Algorithm 2 omits q from its input list but uses it at lines 18 and 20; the experiments on p.8 tune q independently, and this contract explicitly supplies q in (0,1].",
      "The short traces test equations, not Theorem 3.1 convergence, optimal complexity, online stochastic variance, or linear speed-up. eta/gamma/K are algorithm-valid but are not calibrated to the theorem.",
      "The paper gives random historical output; final x_T and network mean(x_T) are not interchangeable with it."
    ]
  },
